                    Offset[{0, 1}, 5], {Center, Top}}, {Center, Bottom}, 
                    "ClosingActions" -> {
                    "ParentChanged", "EvaluatorQuit", "OutsideMouseClick"}]]),
                     Method -> "Preemptive", PassEventsDown -> Automatic, 
                    PassEventsUp -> True}]],
                    DynamicModuleValues:>{}],
                    
                    "# OPF Relative Emergence and Modal Structure Notebook\n\n\
This notebook rebuilds your workflow in a **relative / branch-aware** way and \
fixes the two main issues in the current draft:\n\n1. the background \
substitution did not actually remove derivatives of the fields, so \
[Solve](paclet:ref/Solve) and [Reduce](paclet:ref/Reduce) were being asked to \
solve for constants while derivatives of the original fields were still \
present\n2. the linearization pipeline expanded equations in a way that \
collapsed the first-order system to zeros\n\nIt also adds a **relative \
comparison layer** for the idea that plane-wave modal structure may be \
behaving \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]algorithmically like DNA\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] in the sense of:\n\n- encoded mode coefficients\n- \
branch-dependent activation\n- stable replication of structural patterns \
across scale\n- relative decoherence / measurement dependence\n\nThat analogy \
is kept explicitly separate from direct calculation.\n\n---\n\n## 1. \
Initialization\n\n```wl\nClearAll[\"Global`*\"];\nNeeds[\"VariationalMethods`\
\"];\n\n$HistoryLength = 0;\n\n$Assumptions = \n  Element[{\[Alpha], \[Beta], \
\[Mu], \[CapitalGamma], \[Kappa], \[Sigma], \[Eta], \[CurlyEpsilon], \[Rho]0, \
\[Chi]0, r0, s0, obs0, \[Lambda], \[Omega], kx, ky, kz}, Reals] && \n   \
\[Alpha] > 0 && \[Beta] > 0 && \[Mu] > 0 && \[Lambda] > 0 && \[Chi]0 > 0 && \
\[CapitalGamma] >= 0 && \[Kappa] >= 0 && \[Sigma] >= 0 && \[Eta] >= 0;\n\n\
coords4 = {t, x, y, z};\nspatialCoords = {x, y, z};\nfieldHeads = {\[Rho], \
\[Chi], r, s};\nfieldVars = Through[fieldHeads[t, x, y, z]];\nkSq = kx^2 + \
ky^2 + kz^2;\n\nsay[msg_] := Print[Style[msg, 14, Bold, Darker[Blue]]];\n\
pass[msg_] := Print[Style[\"PASS: \" <> msg, Darker[Green]]];\nfail[msg_] := \
Print[Style[\"FAIL: \" <> msg, Red]];\nwarn[msg_] := Print[Style[\"WARN: \" \
<> msg, Darker[Orange]]];\n\nresidualNorm[exprs_] := \
FullSimplify[Total[Expand[(exprs /. Equal -> Subtract)^2]]];\n\
subtractSides[eq_] := eq /. Equal -> Subtract;\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. \
Interpretive Layer Registry\n\nThese are semantic declarations only.\n\n```wl\
\nlayer0 = <|\n  \"ZeroMeaning\" -> \"UnmeasuredPotential\",\n  \
\"MeasuredZero\" -> \"ObservableNull\",\n  \"TemporalMode\" -> \
\"PremeasurementTimeless\",\n  \"Topology\" -> \"Sphere\",\n  \
\"BoundaryDuality\" -> {0, Infinity},\n  \"Substrate\" -> \
\"LatentInformationalPotential\"\n|>;\n\nlayer1 = <|\n  \"StateVector\" -> \
\[CapitalPsi][\[Rho], \[Chi], r, s],\n  \"Interpretation\" -> \
\"Self-relational pre-stabilized field sector\"\n|>;\n\nlayer2 = <|\n  \
\"Interpretation\" -> \"Measured persistent spacetime sector\",\n  \
\"PersistenceLaw\" -> \"D[field,t] + \[CapitalGamma] field == source\"\n|>;\n\
```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Observation and Relative Stabilization Operators\n\n```wl\
\nlatentZero /: Format[latentZero] := Subscript[0, \"latent\"];\nobservedZero \
/: Format[observedZero] := Subscript[0, \"obs\"];\n\n\
measurementOperator[state_, obsStrength_] := FullSimplify[(1 - \
Exp[-obsStrength]) state];\nunmeasuredComponent[state_, obsStrength_] := \
FullSimplify[Exp[-obsStrength] state];\nstabilizationOperator[state_, \
obsStrength_, \[Gamma]_] := FullSimplify[measurementOperator[state, \
obsStrength]/(1 + \[Gamma])];\n\nobservationalOrder[obs_] := 1 - \
Exp[-\[Kappa] obs];\n\nrelativeObservation[stateA_, stateB_, obsStrength_] := \
\n  FullSimplify[measurementOperator[stateA - stateB, obsStrength]];\n```\n\n\
Checks:\n\n```wl\nsay[\"Observation operator checks:\"];\nPrint[{\n   \
measurementOperator[\[Psi], 0],\n   unmeasuredComponent[\[Psi], 0],\n   \
Limit[measurementOperator[\[Psi], obs], obs -> Infinity, Assumptions -> obs > \
0],\n   observationalOrder[0]\n   } // TableForm];\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. \
Action Density\n\nWe keep the OPF field content but make the definitions \
modular.\n\n```wl\ngradSq4[head_] := Total[D[head[t, x, y, z], #]^2 & /@ \
coords4];\nlaplacian4[expr_] := Total[D[expr, {#, 2}] & /@ coords4];\n\n\
potentialDensity = \n  \[Rho][t, x, y, z] Log[\[Chi][t, x, y, z]] + \n   \
\[Chi][t, x, y, z] r[t, x, y, z]^2 + \n   \[Lambda]/2 s[t, x, y, z]^2 - \n   \
\[Eta] s[t, x, y, z] \[Rho][t, x, y, z];\n\nregularizationDensity = \n  \
\[Alpha]/2 gradSq4[\[Rho]] + \n   \[Beta]/2 gradSq4[\[Chi]] + \n   \[Mu]/2 \
gradSq4[r] + \n   \[Sigma]/2 gradSq4[s];\n\nlagrangianDensity = \
potentialDensity + regularizationDensity;\n\nsay[\"Lagrangian density \
defined.\"];\nPrint[lagrangianDensity // TraditionalForm];\n```\n\n---\n\n## \
5. Euler\[Dash]Lagrange System\n\n```wl\neulerSystem = \
EulerEquations[lagrangianDensity, fieldVars, coords4] // FullSimplify;\n\
eulerLHS = subtractSides /@ eulerSystem;\n\nsay[\"Euler\[Dash]Lagrange \
system:\"];\nPrint[TableForm[eulerSystem]];\n```\n\nFor convenience, also \
store the equations in explicit residual form.\n\n```wl\nresidualAssociation \
= AssociationThread[fieldHeads, eulerLHS];\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Correct \
Constant-Background Reduction\n\nThe key fix is this: for a constant \
background, **all derivatives of the fields vanish**.\n\n```wl\n\
constantBackgroundRules = Dispatch[{\n    \[Rho][t, x, y, z] -> \[Rho]0,\n    \
\[Chi][t, x, y, z] -> \[Chi]0,\n    r[t, x, y, z] -> r0,\n    s[t, x, y, z] \
-> s0,\n    Derivative[__][\[Rho]][__] -> 0,\n    Derivative[__][\[Chi]][__] \
-> 0,\n    Derivative[__][r][__] -> 0,\n    Derivative[__][s][__] -> 0\n    \
}];\n\nbackgroundResiduals = FullSimplify[eulerLHS /. \
constantBackgroundRules];\nbackgroundEquations = Thread[backgroundResiduals \
== 0];\n\nsay[\"Constant-background equations:\"];\n\
Print[TableForm[backgroundEquations]];\n```\n\nNow solve the actual algebraic \
background system.\n\n```wl\nbackgroundSolve = FullSimplify[\n   \
Solve[backgroundEquations, {\[Rho]0, \[Chi]0, r0, s0}, Reals]\n   ];\n\n\
backgroundReduce = FullSimplify[\n   Reduce[backgroundEquations, {\[Rho]0, \
\[Chi]0, r0, s0}, Reals]\n   ];\n\nsay[\"Background Solve output:\"];\n\
Print[backgroundSolve // InputForm];\n\nsay[\"Background Reduce output:\"];\n\
Print[backgroundReduce // InputForm];\n```\n\nUseful branch extraction:\n\n\
```wl\nlatentBranchRules = {r0 -> 0, s0 -> 0};\nlatentBranchConditions = \
FullSimplify[backgroundEquations /. latentBranchRules];\n\n\
stabilizedBranchRules = {r0 -> 0};\nstabilizedBranchSolve = FullSimplify[\n   \
Solve[backgroundEquations /. stabilizedBranchRules, {\[Rho]0, \[Chi]0, s0}, \
Reals]\n   ];\n\nsay[\"Latent branch conditions:\"];\n\
Print[latentBranchConditions // TableForm];\n\nsay[\"Stabilized branch \
candidates:\"];\nPrint[stabilizedBranchSolve // InputForm];\n```\n\nExpected \
algebraic structure:\n\n- from the ``r`` equation, typically ``2 r0 \[Chi]0 \
== 0`` so with ``\[Chi]0 > 0`` one gets ``r0 = 0``\n- the remaining coupled \
sector gives relations among ``\[Rho]0``, ``\[Chi]0``, and ``s0``\n- one \
branch has ``\[Rho]0 = 0``, ``s0 = 0``, ``\[Chi]0 = 1``\n- another branch may \
exist when ``\[Lambda] > 0`` and coupling is strong enough\n\n---\n\n## 7. \
Missing-Variable Audit Relative to Standard Inputs\n\nThis is a symbolic OPF \
audit rather than a physics validation.\n\n```wl\nopfActionVariables = \
DeleteDuplicates @ Cases[\n    lagrangianDensity,\n    _Symbol,\n    Infinity\
\n    ];\n\nstandardLikeConstants = {c, G, \:0127, kB, e, me};\n\
missingRelativeToStandard = Complement[opfActionVariables, \
standardLikeConstants];\n\nsay[\"Missing-variable audit relative to standard \
constant set:\"];\nPrint[missingRelativeToStandard // InputForm];\n```\n\nIf \
you want a tighter audit based on only field/control symbols:\n\n```wl\n\
opfControlSymbols = {\[Alpha], \[Beta], \[Mu], \[Lambda], \[Eta], \[Sigma], \
\[CapitalGamma], \[Kappa]};\nopfFieldSymbols = {\[Rho], \[Chi], r, s};\n\
opfRelativeComplement = Complement[Join[opfControlSymbols, opfFieldSymbols], \
standardLikeConstants];\n\nPrint[opfRelativeComplement // InputForm];\n```\n\n\
---\n\n## 8. Maintenance Dynamics as Layer-2 Persistence\n\nYour original \
maintenance solution simplified incorrectly because of branch handling with \
[UnitStep](paclet:ref/UnitStep). Use a piecewise-safe derivation.\n\n```wl\n\
obsProfile[t_] := obs0 UnitStep[t];\nmeasurementSource[t_] := \
observationalOrder[obsProfile[t]];\n\nmaintenanceEquation[field_] := \
D[field[t], t] + \[CapitalGamma] field[t] == measurementSource[t];\n\n\
maintenanceSolution = FullSimplify[\n   DSolveValue[{maintenanceEquation[\
\[Phi]], \[Phi][0] == 0}, \[Phi], t],\n   Assumptions -> $Assumptions && t > \
0\n   ];\n\nsay[\"Maintenance solution for t > 0:\"];\n\
Print[maintenanceSolution // TraditionalForm];\n```\n\nThe expected \
simplified form for ``t > 0`` is:\n\n$$\n\\phi(t)=\\frac{1-e^{-\\kappa \\, \
obs0}}{\\Gamma}\\left(1-e^{-\\Gamma t}\\right)\n$$\n\nYou can verify \
directly:\n\n```wl\nmaintenanceResidual = FullSimplify[\n   \
(D[maintenanceSolution[t], t] + \[CapitalGamma] maintenanceSolution[t] - \
measurementSource[t]),\n   Assumptions -> $Assumptions && t > 0\n   ];\n\n\
Print[maintenanceResidual];\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9. Spacetime-Stabilization \
Surrogate Extraction\n\nInstead of selecting the first equation containing \
``s``, explicitly extract the ``s`` equation.\n\n```wl\nspacetimeResidual = \
residualAssociation[s];\nspacetimeEquation = spacetimeResidual == 0;\n\n\
say[\"Spacetime-stabilization surrogate equation:\"];\n\
Print[spacetimeEquation // TraditionalForm];\n```\n\nThis is the direct \
Layer-1 to Layer-2 surrogate for stabilization.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Correct \
Linearization Around a Background\n\nThe robust way is:\n\n1. substitute \
perturbed fields\n2. expand in ``\[CurlyEpsilon]``\n3. use background \
equations to cancel order-0 terms\n4. extract order-1 terms only\n\n```wl\n\
perturbationRules = {\n   \[Rho] -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, \[Rho]0 + \
\[CurlyEpsilon] u[tt, xx, yy, zz]],\n   \[Chi] -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, \
\[Chi]0 + \[CurlyEpsilon] v[tt, xx, yy, zz]],\n   r -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, \
zz}, r0 + \[CurlyEpsilon] w[tt, xx, yy, zz]],\n   s -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, \
zz}, s0 + \[CurlyEpsilon] q[tt, xx, yy, zz]]\n   };\n\nexpandedResiduals = \
Normal[Series[#, {\[CurlyEpsilon], 0, 1}]] & /@ (eulerLHS /. \
perturbationRules);\nbackgroundOrder0 = FullSimplify[Coefficient[#, \
\[CurlyEpsilon], 0] & /@ expandedResiduals];\nlinearOrder1 = \
FullSimplify[Coefficient[#, \[CurlyEpsilon], 1] & /@ expandedResiduals];\n\n\
backgroundRulesFromSolve = backgroundSolve /. RuleDelayed -> Rule;\n\n\
say[\"Zeroth-order background residuals:\"];\nPrint[backgroundOrder0 // \
TableForm];\n\nsay[\"First-order linearized residuals:\"];\n\
Print[linearOrder1 // TableForm];\n```\n\nIf you want the linearization about \
the latent branch specifically:\n\n```wl\nlatentBackground = {\[Rho]0 -> 0, \
\[Chi]0 -> 1, r0 -> 0, s0 -> 0};\nlatentLinearSystem = \
FullSimplify[linearOrder1 /. latentBackground];\n\nsay[\"Linearized system \
about latent branch:\"];\nPrint[latentLinearSystem // TableForm];\n```\n\nFor \
this branch, the expected structure is approximately:\n\n```wl\n\
expectedLatentLinear = {\n   v - \[Alpha] laplacian4[u[t, x, y, z]],\n   u + \
\[Beta] laplacian4[v[t, x, y, z]],\n   \[Mu] laplacian4[w[t, x, y, z]] - 2 \
w[t, x, y, z],\n   \[Sigma] laplacian4[q[t, x, y, z]] - \[Lambda] q[t, x, y, \
z] + \[Eta] u[t, x, y, z]\n   };\n```\n\nYou can compare with:\n\n```wl\n\
FullSimplify[latentLinearSystem - expectedLatentLinear]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 11. \
Plane-Wave Modal Reduction\n\nNow the modal reduction will no longer collapse \
trivially.\n\n```wl\nplaneRules = {\n   u -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, u0 \
Exp[I (kx xx + ky yy + kz zz - \[Omega] tt)]],\n   v -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, \
zz}, v0 Exp[I (kx xx + ky yy + kz zz - \[Omega] tt)]],\n   w -> Function[{tt, \
xx, yy, zz}, w0 Exp[I (kx xx + ky yy + kz zz - \[Omega] tt)]],\n   q -> \
Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, q0 Exp[I (kx xx + ky yy + kz zz - \[Omega] tt)]]\n \
  };\n\nlatentModalAlgebraic = FullSimplify[\n   (latentLinearSystem /. \
planeRules)/Exp[I (kx x + ky y + kz z - \[Omega] t)]\n   ];\n\nsay[\"Latent \
modal algebraic system:\"];\nPrint[latentModalAlgebraic // TableForm];\n```\n\
\nConstruct the modal matrix explicitly.\n\n```wl\nmodeAmplitudes = {u0, v0, \
w0, q0};\nlatentStiffnessMatrix = \
FullSimplify[CoefficientArrays[latentModalAlgebraic, modeAmplitudes][[2]]];\n\
latentDispersionDet = FullSimplify[Det[latentStiffnessMatrix]];\n\n\
say[\"Latent stiffness matrix:\"];\nPrint[MatrixForm[latentStiffnessMatrix]];\
\n\nsay[\"Latent dispersion determinant:\"];\nPrint[latentDispersionDet // \
TraditionalForm];\n```\n\nFor the latent branch with the Euclideanized \
4-Laplacian convention used above, one typically gets factors of the form\n\n\
$$\n\\alpha \\beta (k_x^2+k_y^2+k_z^2+\\omega^2)^2-1\n$$\n\nfor the coupled \
``u,v`` sector, plus independent factors for ``w`` and ``q``. That is a \
precise place to test your \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]algorithmic encoding\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] intuition.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Stable Frequency \
Extraction\n\nFollowing your OPF directive, isolate undamped harmonic modes \
by solving for purely oscillatory branches.\n\n```wl\nlatentEigenvalues = \
Eigenvalues[latentStiffnessMatrix] // FullSimplify;\n\nsay[\"Modal \
eigenvalues:\"];\nPrint[latentEigenvalues // TableForm];\n```\n\nFrequency \
candidates from determinant zero:\n\n```wl\nomegaSolutions = FullSimplify[\n  \
 Solve[latentDispersionDet == 0, \[Omega], Reals]\n   ];\n\nsay[\"Real \
frequency branches from determinant zero:\"];\nPrint[omegaSolutions // \
InputForm];\n```\n\nIf you want strictly oscillatory modes with real positive \
frequency:\n\n```wl\nstableFrequencyCandidates = Select[\n   \[Omega] /. \
omegaSolutions,\n   FullSimplify[Im[#] == 0 && Re[#] > 0] &\n   ];\n\n\
Print[stableFrequencyCandidates // InputForm];\n```\n\n---\n\n## 13. Relative \
Branch Comparison\n\nThis section compares latent and stabilized backgrounds \
as **relative sectors**.\n\n```wl\nrelativeBranchDifference[expr_, branchA_, \
branchB_] := FullSimplify[(expr /. branchA) - (expr /. branchB)];\n\n\
latentBranch = {\[Rho]0 -> 0, \[Chi]0 -> 1, r0 -> 0, s0 -> 0};\n\n\
stabilizedBranchSymbolic = FirstCase[\n   backgroundSolve,\n   rules_List /; \
FreeQ[r0 /. rules, _Symbol?(# === r0 &)],\n   \
Missing[\"NoConcreteStabilizedBranch\"]\n   ];\n\nsay[\"Relative branch \
comparison object:\"];\nPrint[stabilizedBranchSymbolic // InputForm];\n```\n\n\
Compare modal determinants if a nontrivial stabilized branch is available.\n\n\
```wl\nIf[stabilizedBranchSymbolic === \
Missing[\"NoConcreteStabilizedBranch\"],\n  warn[\"No explicit stabilized \
branch extracted symbolically.\"],\n  Module[{stabilizedLinearSystem, \
stabilizedModalAlgebraic, stabilizedMatrix, stabilizedDet},\n   \
stabilizedLinearSystem = FullSimplify[linearOrder1 /. \
stabilizedBranchSymbolic];\n   stabilizedModalAlgebraic = \
FullSimplify[(stabilizedLinearSystem /. planeRules)/Exp[I (kx x + ky y + kz z \
- \[Omega] t)]];\n   stabilizedMatrix = \
FullSimplify[CoefficientArrays[stabilizedModalAlgebraic, \
modeAmplitudes][[2]]];\n   stabilizedDet = \
FullSimplify[Det[stabilizedMatrix]];\n   say[\"Relative determinant shift \
(stabilized - latent):\"];\n   Print[FullSimplify[stabilizedDet - \
latentDispersionDet] // TraditionalForm];\n   ]\n  ];\n```\n\n---\n\n## 14. \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]DNA-like\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] Analogy Layer, Kept \
Separate from Direct Physics\n\nThis section is interpretive only. It does \
**not** claim biological identity.\n\n### Directly calculable objects\n\n- \
background branches\n- linear response operators\n- stiffness matrices\n- \
determinant factorization\n- stable frequency sets\n- relative sensitivity to \
observation/stabilization parameters\n\n### Analogy-only structural \
similarities\n\n- modal coefficients as symbolic \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]alphabet\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]\n- determinant \
factorization as grammar / constraint structure\n- branch selection as \
context-dependent expression\n- persistence under maintenance as \
replication-like stability\n- scale-relative activation as regulatory-like \
behavior\n\nYou can package this separation explicitly:\n\n```wl\n\
relativeInterpretationRegistry = <|\n  \"DirectCalculation\" -> <|\n    \
\"BackgroundBranches\" -> backgroundSolve,\n    \"LatentLinearSystem\" -> \
latentLinearSystem,\n    \"LatentStiffnessMatrix\" -> latentStiffnessMatrix,\n\
    \"LatentDispersionDeterminant\" -> latentDispersionDet,\n    \
\"StableFrequencies\" -> omegaSolutions\n    |>,\n  \"AnalogyOnly\" -> <|\n   \
 \"AlphabetLike\" -> \"Mode amplitudes {u0,v0,w0,q0}\",\n    \"GrammarLike\" \
-> \"Factorization constraints of determinant\",\n    \"ExpressionLike\" -> \
\"Observation/stabilization dependent branch activation\",\n    \
\"ReplicationLike\" -> \"Persistent modal structure under maintenance flow\"\n\
    |>\n  |>;\n\nPrint[relativeInterpretationRegistry // InputForm];\n```\n\n\
---\n\n## 15. Dimensional and Structural Validation Hooks\n\nIf you want a \
dimensionless reformulation, see \
[NondimensionalizationTransform](paclet:ref/NondimensionalizationTransform).\n\
\nFor inactive PDE inspection workflows, see [Inactive](paclet:ref/Inactive).\
\n\nFor consistency checks, you can define residual validators:\n\n```wl\n\
validateResidualZero[expr_] := TrueQ[FullSimplify[expr == 0]];\n\n\
latentResidualCheck = FullSimplify[\n   latentModalAlgebraic /. \
Thread[modeAmplitudes -> ConstantArray[0, Length[modeAmplitudes]]]\n   ];\n\n\
say[\"Latent residual zero-mode check:\"];\nPrint[latentResidualCheck // \
TableForm];\n```\n\nYou may also want to nondimensionalize the PDE system \
before modal comparison.\n\n---\n\n## 16. Full L0 -> L1 -> L2 Pipeline Object\
\n\n```wl\nopfPipeline = <|\n  \"Layer0\" -> layer0,\n  \"Layer1\" -> <|\n    \
\"LagrangianDensity\" -> lagrangianDensity,\n    \"EulerSystem\" -> \
eulerSystem,\n    \"BackgroundSolve\" -> backgroundSolve,\n    \
\"LinearizedLatentSystem\" -> latentLinearSystem,\n    \
\"LatentStiffnessMatrix\" -> latentStiffnessMatrix,\n    \
\"LatentDispersionDeterminant\" -> latentDispersionDet\n    |>,\n  \"Layer2\" \
-> <|\n    \"ObservationOrder\" -> observationalOrder[obs],\n    \
\"MaintenanceEquation\" -> maintenanceEquation[\[Phi]],\n    \
\"MaintenanceSolution\" -> maintenanceSolution[t],\n    \"SpacetimeEquation\" \
-> spacetimeEquation\n    |>,\n  \"RelativeInterpretation\" -> \
relativeInterpretationRegistry\n|>;\n\nsay[\"Pipeline object assembled.\"];\n\
Print[opfPipeline // InputForm];\n```\n\n---\n\n## 17. Suggested Next \
Extensions\n\n1. **Nondimensionalize** the field equations using \
[NondimensionalizationTransform](paclet:ref/NondimensionalizationTransform)\n\
2. **Factor** the modal determinant over specific branches and parameter \
regimes\n3. **Add damping / true time asymmetry** if you want physical \
stability instead of symmetric 4-gradient regularization\n4. **Introduce a \
true measurement coupling term** into the action rather than only the Layer-2 \
maintenance equation\n5. **Compare branch spectra** under different \
observation strengths\n6. **Build test surrogates** for double-slit-style \
context dependence and scale-relative decoherence\n\n---\n\n## 18. Minimal \
Execution Order\n\n```wl\nsay[\"Run order:\"];\nPrint[\n Column[{\n   \"1. \
Evaluate sections 1-6 to get corrected backgrounds\",\n   \"2. Evaluate \
section 8 for maintenance dynamics\",\n   \"3. Evaluate sections 10-12 for \
corrected modal structure\",\n   \"4. Evaluate section 13 for relative branch \
comparison\",\n   \"5. Use section 14 only for analogy-safe interpretation\"\n\
   }]\n ];\n```\n\n---\n\n## 19. Expected Main Correction Relative to Your \
Current Notebook\n\nYour previous modal determinant became zero because the \
linearized residuals were already zero. That happened because the background \
and perturbation substitution pipeline was not isolating the first-order \
terms correctly.\n\nThis notebook fixes that by:\n\n- applying proper \
constant-background derivative rules\n- extracting residuals explicitly\n- \
separating zeroth and first order in ``\[CurlyEpsilon]``\n- only then \
applying the plane-wave ansatz\n- constructing the modal matrix with \
[CoefficientArrays](paclet:ref/CoefficientArrays)\n\nSo if the plane-wave \
structure looks \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]DNA-like\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] to \
you, this version gives a rigorous place to test exactly **which algebraic \
structures repeat, stabilize, factor, and branch**.",
                    SelectWithContents->True]}
